Code derived from R08 Access Bridge
-----------------------------------

R08 Access Bridge (https://github.com/Anezium/R08-Access-Bridge), Copyright Anezium. The
glasses' input, navigation, settings screen and self-arm are derived from it and modified for
the Meta Neural Band and Lumen's grid, in app/src/main/java/dev/lumen/glasses/:
AccessibilityNavigator, AccessibilityWindowRoots, LauncherNavigator, GestureDispatcher,
GlassesAction, RokidSystemActions, BandAccessibilityService, MainActivity, BootReceiver,
BridgeCommandActivity, BridgeProtocol, PrivilegedShortcutBridge, LocalSelfArmStatus,
SelfArmController, SelfArmLocalAdbBootstrapper, SelfArmWirelessAdbController,
SelfArmWirelessDebuggingAutomator, SelfArmSettingsTextMatcher, and the ReadEra, ArBook and
NewPipe compatibility modes (ReaderaCompatibility, ArbookCompatibility, NewPipeCompatibility);
and the helper scripts in tools/.

R08 Access Bridge's repository does not state a license. Its author has not granted one for
this project yet; the terms are being arranged with him and will be recorded here. This code is
not covered by Rokid Lumen's MIT License. If you are Anezium and want anything changed, open an
issue or contact the maintainer.

Thanks to Anezium for R08 Access Bridge: it showed that the Rokid glasses can be driven through
an accessibility service and armed from the glasses themselves, and most of what makes Lumen
usable day to day comes from it. Thanks also for Rokid Nexus, credited above.

rokid-r08-wake (https://github.com/hacha/rokid-r08-wake), Copyright (c) 2026 hacha, MIT
License (LICENSE-rokid-r08-wake): the loopback self-arm technique that R08 Access Bridge's
accessibility watchdog recovery, and so Lumen's, is built on. A short part of SelfArmController
follows its SelfArm code.
